A||N||3||Dreamer||85 2.5 conversion to 2.8 or 3800||||1||
Z||000000||Dreamer||01-23-2001||10:22 PM||||Ihave been reading that there is a difference in the 85 wiring. Is this true? I want to do a conversion to a 2.8 or a 3800. I know I need a Fuel pump. radiator, flywheel( I think) wiring harness from the v-6donor. Is this an easy swap? Is the motor carriage the same as other years? any advice would be great. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||01-23-2001||11:10 PM||||The 84 had wiring for a 4 cylinder engine.  All other years had the potential for a v6. If you stick to the Fiero 2.8 v6, it should fit in with few problems.  So if you have an 85 or newer, no problems.  If you go to a different engine 3.1, 3.4, 3800 and you haven't done this work before, get professional help.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Dreamer||01-23-2001||11:32 PM||||I am a mechanic, I just need to know what type of wiring nightmares I am getting into. I dont care what it takes it has to be done. Thanks for your advice.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>The 84 had wiring for a 4 cylinder engine.  All other years had the potential for a v6. If you stick to the Fiero 2.8 v6, it should fit in with few problems.  So if you have an 85 or newer, no problems.  If you go to a different engine 3.1, 3.4, 3800 and you haven't done this work before, get professional help.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||01-24-2001||08:21 AM||||You'll need the complete wiring harness from the donor car, get the transmission too.  You'll need a new fuel pump, 84 fuel pump doesn't run at the right pressure for larger engines. The gas tank for the 84 is not interchangable with other Fiero years, so you'll be stuck with a small gas tank (8 gal I think).  You'll need the wiring diagrams for the front of the 84 and match up the later engine's wires to the 84 wires.  You may need to weld in transmission supports depending on transmission used.  You should get the ECM from the donor car.<P>If you're a mechanic all this nightmare is a no brainer.||||reg||3
